    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0425" n="329" xml:id="pg329"/>

                <head>No. 256.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turner to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monrovia, Liberia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">Jan</hi>. 24, 1872</date>.
                        (Received Feb. 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint the Department
                    with the fact that Hon. J. J. Roberts was inaugurated President of the republic
                    of Liberia on the 1st day of January, 1872. The term of office for the President
                    is two years, and this is the fifth time that his excellency President Roberts
                    has been elected President of Liberia. The occasion seemed one of general
                    interest; quietude prevailed; persons from all sections of the country were
                    present. Having been unable to procure a manuscript copy of the President’s
                    inaugural address, I am forced to forward by this mail printed copies
                    thereof.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. MILTON TURNER.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
